Z||000000||Wannabe||06-14-2000||09:38 AM||||Anyone in Southern Ontario or upstate NY might want to check this out. We have rented the Shannonville Pro track for the day on Sunday July 16. Anyone who's wanted to try out their Fiero on a race track, this will be an excellent opportunity to do it in an environment that won't be too intimdating for novices, and won't be to crowded for those with more experience(45 participants max). Shannonville is a great place to learn, flat with lots of run off area, but many challenging turns. You can get some info on the track at <A HREF="http://www.shannonville.com" TARGET=_blank>www.shannonville.com</A>   Contact me if you are interested in attending and to book your spot. $250CDN gets you lapping from 9:00AM to 5:00PM, lunch and informal instruction for novices.  The track is booked for the entire season, so there aren't many opportunities to do this! See ya at the track!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000001||BlackGT||06-14-2000||02:26 PM||||Now why is it that when I lived in God forsaken "Upstate New York" no one saw<BR>or even heard of a Fiero, couldn`t find <BR>one to buy and people would scream if you<BR>said you would like to take a car on a race track......I move to Atlanta, find the Fiero I want and live about an hours drive from Road Atlanta and now someone is organizing<BR>a race day at a track in my home state in my<BR>favorite car after I leave! It just ain`t fair...... ||||reg||1
